    "description": "Mineral, Gemstone, and Fossil Specimen Collection Lot\nEarth Science Lapidary and Rockhounding Assortment\nThis diverse collection includes an assortment of polished tumbled stones, rough mineral specimens, natural fossil shark teeth, and lapidary pieces. The lot features an educational Polished Gemstones of the World labeled display case, a dyed teal agate slice, an open quartz crystalline geode half, and a small grooved wooden sorting tray.\nItems Included:\nCased \"Polished Gemstones of the World\" identification set with various mineral specimens\nNatural fossilized shark teeth in various sizes\nCut and polished teal blue agate slab slice with outer rind\nHollow quartz geode section showing interior crystal formation\nAssorted tumbled rocks, jasper, agates, quartz, and engraved stones\nTwo bags containing rough and chipped mineral fragments\nWooden display tray with centimeter scale\nCondition:\nNatural specimens show inherent variations, inclusions, and matrix textures. Polished stones show smooth tumbled finishes with light handling wear. Shark teeth show typical fossilized wear, with some tip or root erosion. Plastic display box has minor surface scratching and scuffs. Wooden tray has minor cosmetic marks.\nThank you for all of your support!",
    "score_reasons": [
      "Opportunity term 'collection' in description (+7)",
